## Integrity/hardening concern

Several application-managed files are written directly with `fs::write`. Direct writes can leave truncated files after crashes or disk-full errors and follow a pre-existing final-component symlink.

Relevant locations include:
- `src/assets.rs` bundled-font cache writes;
- `src/ui/theme.rs` settings, custom theme, and source-style writes;
- `src/ui/window.rs` GTK bookmark writes.

## Proposed work

- Introduce a shared atomic-write helper:
  - create a unique temporary file in the same directory;
  - use restrictive permissions;
  - write and flush successfully;
  - atomically rename into place;
  - reject unsafe symlink/non-regular-file destinations where appropriate.
- Preserve the previous valid file when serialization or writing fails.
- Consider directory ownership/permissions before writing application-managed cache/config data.

## Acceptance criteria

- Interrupted or failed writes preserve the previous valid file.
- Application-managed writes do not follow a substituted final-component symlink.
- Newly created private configuration/cache files use appropriate permissions.
- Tests cover disk/write failure and symlink destinations.

